  "id": "nsw_planning_doc_033",
  "text": "Planning Document: Marrickville DCP 2011 - 9 16 Abergeldie Estate\n\nClause 9.16.1 - heritage (heritage): The precinct contains The Abergeldie Estate Heritage Conservation Area.\n\nClause 9.16.1 - parking (development_control): Off street parking is typically a side driveway except where lots are too small and onstreet parking prevails (for example, parts of Union, Arlington and Abergeldie Streets).\n\nClause 9.16.2 - heritage (heritage): To protect and preserve the identified period buildings within the precinct and encourage their sympathetic alteration or restoration.\n\nClause 9.16.2 - heritage (heritage): To protect the identified Heritage Items within the precinct.\n\nClause 9.16.2 - height_limit (development_control): To maintain distinctly single storey streetscapes that exist within the precinct.\n\nClause 9.16.2 - heritage (heritage): To protect groups or runs of buildings which retain their original form including roof forms, original detailing and finishes.\n\nClause 9.16.2 - heritage (heritage): To protect significant streetscape s and/or public domain elements within the precinct including landscaping, fencing, open space, sandstone kerbing and guttering, views and vistas and prevailing subdivision patterns.\n\nClause 9.16.2 - zoning (land_use_zoning): To preserve the predominantly low density residential character of the precinct.\n\n",
  "metadata": {
    "document_name": "Marrickville DCP 2011 - 9 16 Abergeldie Estate",
